      en: "The Military Cemetery in Barbados was established in the 19th century to inter British soldiers stationed on the island during the colonial period. It contains graves from the Napoleonic Wars and both World Wars. The headstones feature a mix of Victorian symbolism and military honours. The cemetery is located near the Garrison Savannah, a historic parade ground. Many of those buried died from tropical diseases such as yellow fever. Maintenance is carried out by the Commonwealth War Graves Commission, ensuring the graves are preserved. The site stands as a quiet testament to the imperial past and the human costs of colonial governance.",
