      en: "Rock Hall Free Village was established after the abolition of slavery in 1834 by freed slaves. It was one of the first free settlements in Barbados. Residents purchased plots through communal savings and built their own houses and churches. The village developed a strong agricultural base, primarily through sugarcane and vegetable cultivation. The community maintained its own education and social welfare system. Today, Rock Hall symbolises the struggle for freedom and self-reliance. Some original stone houses survive, bearing witness to the nascent independence of former slaves.",
