      en: "Blackman's Gully Bridge is a historic stone bridge in St. John Parish, Barbados. Built in the 18th century, it spans a deep gully. The bridge was constructed by enslaved Africans and is a testament to colonial engineering. It is one of the few surviving bridges from that era on the island. Surrounded by tropical forest, the area is popular for hiking. The bridge is a protected heritage structure.",
